1. The Contractor undertakes to comply with all applicable requirements of  the Employer in the field of quality of maintenance of work sites of capital construction facilities set forth in this Appendix to the Standard, with which the responsible representative of the Employer has made the Contractor aware.
2. These requirements do not apply to the conduct of  work:
- In underground conditions (except for the Employer's infrastructure on the surface);
- In the shops in operation;
- On  the  construction  of linear  objects,  including  power  lines,  communications,  trunk (  external) pipelines for various purposes and other similar facilities;
- On construction of facilities located in the right-of-way (right-of-way) of railroads and highways and other transport routes located outside the Employer's work site.
3. The Contractor undertakes to  ensure the implementation of the necessary measures to ensure the following quality requirements for the maintenance of the work site.

At the  entrance  (entrance)  to  the  construction  site,  in  the  visibility area,  there  shall  be  an information  board  with  the  following  information:  the  name  of the  reconstruction/construction facility,  the name of the Employer and Contractor, telephone numbers, positions and names of the responsible workmen, the planned start and end dates of  reconstruction/construction (the recommended format of the Information Board in Appendix 8 to this Standard).
The size, possible design features of  the Information Board and methods of  its installation shall be determined by the Contractor depending on the peculiarities of  the work site.
- 3.2  Scheme of safe movement of vehicles and routes for pedestrians on the working site of the capital construction project
At the entrance to the construction site, in the visibility area, a "Traffic diagram of vehicles and  pedestrian  routes  on the  working  site  of the  capital  construction  project"  shall  be  installed, containing:
- permitted routes for vehicle and pedestrian traffic on the work site;
- road signs regulating traffic;
- places where vehicles and pedestrians cross each other and hazardous areas;
- permitted places for parking and washing of  vehicles;
- the permitted maximum speed of vehicles;
- the place of  exit from the work site.
The recommended format of "Schemes of safe vehicle traffic and pedestrian routes on the working site of  the capital construction facility" is shown in Appendix 9 to this Standard.

The Contractor's construction headquarters shall be in the form of a container-type modular building,  unless  otherwise specified  in the construction organization project  and/or  the Employer's requirements. The size/size and number of  floors of  the building shall be determined by the Contractor based  on  his  need  for  the  number  of workplaces  for  managers  and  specialists  engaged  by  the Contractor to organize and support the contract work.
The following rooms shall be arranged in the Contractor's construction headquarters:
- Meeting room (intended use - production meetings, briefings, staff meetings);
- Rooms I "open spaces" for the work of  managers and specialists of  the Contractor;
- Restrooms;
- Rooms for the archive of  documents;
- Warehouse inventory, clothing and personal protective equipment;
- The rooms for meals (provided that such rooms are not provided by the Employer).

Must be provided with the following information materials posted on the stands:
- Information plate with contact information of  key employees of  the Employer, Contractor, Subcontractors (full name, position, contact information (phone number, e-mail);
- Information plate with the name of  the person responsible for fire safety;
- The master plan of  the building (graphic part with explications);
- Construction plan, graphic part with explications for all stages I stages of construction / reconstruction);
- Up-to-date schedule of  works on construction sites with the main milestones and updated fact on the reporting date;
- Staff  mobilization schedule and a schedule of the need for machines and mechanisms;
At the request of  the Employer must be equipped with equipment for audio/video conferences.
The offices/"open spaces" for the work of the Contractor's managers and specialists shall be equipped with communication equipment, computers with Internet access, and printing devices.

The  Contractor/Subcontractor  camp  must  be  equipped in accordance with  the construction organization project, current requirements of  sanitary regulations and fire safety rules of Kazakhstan.
Prior to commencing work on the equipment of  the camp, the Contractor, in order to coordinate with the Employer the possibility of  bringing mobile living quarters to the worksite, shall present the mobile  living  quarters to the Employer's representative to assess  and  inspect  the  overall  technical condition, compliance with sanitary and fire safety standards.
Prior to the placement of  Contractor/Subcontractor personnel in the camp, the Contractor shall develop detailed plans of the camp with the layout, types of  structures, their dimensions, dimensions of rooms within them, connections to utilities, approaches and entrances.
The  camp  area  and  all  living  quarters  within  it  should  be  decorated  with  appropriate inscriptions and signs (Contractor/Subcontractor name, purpose of  the rooms, responsible persons for fire safety, evacuation routes, etc.).
The typical composition of  the premises of the camp:
- The room for the OHS classes;
- Checkrooms;
- Room for rest and warming of workers;
- Shower room, washroom;

There must be places for smoking:
- Located in close proximity, at a safe distance from each of the work areas outside the work area;
- Equipped with canopies of non-combustible materials, benches and garbage cans;
- Marked  by  appropriate signs and information  boards, primary  fire  extinguishing equipment;
Smoking outside organized places is prohibited.

The work site area, including the territory of the workers' camps, passageways, passageways, sites  for  storage  and  consolidated  assembly of structures  and  elements,  workplaces,  as  well as the surrounding area must be kept clean and tidy. To this end:
- During the warm season, roads and driveways should be cleaned as needed with a water washer,  and  process  roads  are  regularly  sprayed  with  water  or  bituminous  emulsions  for  dust suppression;
- During the cold season, roads and passages are cleaned with snow removal equipment at a frequency that ensures its serviceability;
- Construction debris, household waste and snow are removed from the work site in a timely manner.

