7. Rj - the share of the payroll of Kazakhstani  personnel in the total payroll of the supplier or subcontractor, performing the j contract, is calculated by the following formula:
Rj = SFRK/SF
Where:
Salary Foundation of RK (SFRK) is the payroll of  the Kazakhstani personnel of  the supplier or subcontractor performing the j contract for the period of the j-contract;
Salary  Foundation  (SF)  is  the  total  payroll  of  the  supplier's  or  subcontractor's  employees performing the j contract for the period of  the j contract.
Branches (representative offices) oflegal entities are not suppliers or subcontractors.

To evaluate the technical part of the Tender offer, the Contractor must provide the following documentation:
- Work schedule;
- Receiving LTSA offers from manufacturers of the main critical equipment, within 12 and 27 years from the expiration date of the warranty period. The Participant is obliged to conclude service and maintenance agreements with the Customer during its warranty period - 2 years;
- The Supply Specification (delivery set) of the energy source that is clarified/specified by the Contractor  (a  complete  list  of  supplied  equipment,  utilities,  communication  systems,  inventory, materials, products, structures, works, services, indicating types, main technical characteristics, weight, and so on);
- Preliminary Master Plan within (the allocated by the Customer) construction site, proposed by the Contractor;
- Updated title list of  buildings and structures;
- Layout drawings of  the placement of  energy source equipment in buildings and structures;
- A general PI diagram of  the Main body of  the energy source, a schematic diagram of  the output of electric power of  the energy source including Switchgears of own needs (RUSN), a block diagram of the automation of the energy source;
- Drawings of  the general type of  the proposed equipment (with overall, installation, connection dimensions, weight) and specifications;
installations (Gas Turbine,  HRSG, Steam Turbine) in various modes (10%, 20%, 30%, 50%, 75%, 100%) and at different outdoor temperatures, taking into account the height of  the construction site
- Aerodynamic, hydraulic and thermal calculation of energy above sea level;
- Correlation curves in order to adjust the test results to the standard conditions (according to ISO), local conditions and to the nominal conditions with respect to the turbine gas temperature;
- Dependence of  the nominal base and peak power and efficiency of  the gas turbine, the flow rate and temperature of  the gases behind the turbines on the ambient air temperature;
- -Dependences  of  fuel  consumption  (CCGT efficiency, gas  consumption  and  outdoor temperature) on electrical load;
- -Formulae  and  diagrams  showing  the  change  in  recommended  operating  hours  between mandatory inspections/major repairs, depending on the number of emergency shutdowns and startups, operating hours at base load and continuous operation at peak load;
- -Technical  description  of all  the  equipment  of the  energy  source  with  indication  of the characteristics of energy efficiency;
- Correlation diagrams of the energy source parameters against external conditions;
- Schedules of energy source start-ups at various states;
- Noise characteristics of  the main equipment;
- Environmental indicators of energy source emissions;
- Conditions for the implementation of  technological protections, locks, automatic reserve input (A  VR), technological and emergency alarms
