The selection of water samples from the Badam reservoir is given. For a rational water treatment scheme, it is necessary to conduct additional analyzes during the annual period.
Due to the high demand for water resources in  this region and the further increase in  water consumption for irrigation of agricultural land, there is a shortage of free volumes in the reservoir.
In this connection, the Badam-Sairam groundwater deposit was determined as a reserve source of water for the Facility. Located in the middle reaches of  the r. Badam,  1.5 km southeast of Shymkent. Groundwater is fresh, with a mineralization of  0.  76-0.9 g/1, sulfate-bicarbonate, sodium-calcium.
Water intake facilities are envisaged with a capacity of 16.80 thousand m 3 /day, 4900.0 thousand m 3 /year from a network of artesian wells, water storage tanks and a pumping station.
At the design stage, it is necessary to re-evaluate groundwater reserves.
The following water supply systems are considered at the power plant site:
- technical water supply;
- -household and drinking;
- -production and fire fighting.
At the projected site of the power plant,  water is used for household and drinking needs, fire fighting, watering green spaces and roads.
The maximum consumption of initial water of the designed power plant will be 700.0 m 3 /hour, 4900.0 thousand m 3 /year, including:
- 525.0 m 3 /h - at the boiler feeding WTP;
- 120.0 m 3 /hour - for drinking water treatment;
- 48.5 m 3 /hour - to replenish the fire-fighting water supply in the tanks in case of  fire;
- 6.5 m 3 /hour - for watering green spaces and roads.

The total consumption of  cooling water in the cooling system of  steam turbine condensers and auxiliary equipment of  the Facility, according to the considered options, is 56,000.0 m 3 /h. To cool the circulating water, you will need:
- -evaporative  cooling  towers  with  an  irrigation  area  of 3x2100  m 2 , while  the  frequency  of irrigation in the condensing mode will be 8.9 m 3 /m 2 ·hour;
- circulation pumping station with a capacity of  56,000.0 m 3 /h with a switching chamber and a suction chamber;
- circulation conduits with a diameter of  1600+  2400 mm made of  steel pipes with stiffening rings. To  recharge  the  circulating system, water will be  required in  the  amount of 1100.0  m 3 /hour, 7700.0 thousand m 3 /year.
An evaporation field of  about 150 ha will be required to utilize the circulatory system blowdown water.
Taking into account the shortage of water resources in the region under consideration, a dry condenser was considered for cooling the installed equipment. When installing a dry condenser, water is not required to feed the cooling system.

The following water disposal systems are provided at the power plant site:
- household sewerage;
- -sewerage of  industrial effluents;
- -sewerage of  emergency drain of  transformer oil.
Due to the small amount of  precipitation and the significant evaporation capacity of  the area, as well as taking into account the soils that make up the site - sands, an open rainwater collection system with subsequent evaporation is provided at the power plant site.

- high energy efficiency;
- high reliability and operational readiness for work;
- high degree of automation;
- the level of emissions into the atmosphere in accordance with the norms of the Republic of Kazakhstan;
- low cost of  maintenance;
- suitability for repair at the installation site in accordance with the regulations established by the equipment manufacturer;
- the total electric power of  the power plant on the high voltage side (  excluding the power plant's own needs) must be at least 1000 MW, taking into account climatic conditions, geographical location, ground level above sea level, seismic activity level and other characteristics of  the construction site;
- electric installed capacity of  each power unit - to be determined by the project.
- the rate of output of the available power (taking into account the work on the bypass chimney and taking into account seasonal, regime and repair restrictions) of  the power plant to the network from the moment the «Start» command is received is at least 10 MW/min, regardless of the thermal state of the unit (s);
- -power  plant  control  ranges  must  correspond  to  the  lower  limit  within  the  technical  and technological minimums;
- the scheme for connecting the units to the electrical network, as well as the features of the operation of the auxiliary equipment of the power plant should not lead to a limitation in the output of power from more than one power unit during maintenance;
- decrease in the rated power of  the units during their operation during the overhaul period should not exceed 4%, and the decrease in electrical EF should not exceed 2% (relative). Ensuring the possibility of  carrying out all types of  inspections (repairs) at the place of  operation of  the equipment. The increase in specific fuel consumption should not exceed 2% during the overhaul period. The restoration of the specified indicators after the overhaul should be ensured.
- capacity limitation depending on the weather conditions typical for  the construction site no more than 15% of the installed capacity. Data on weather conditions in accordance with CIT PK 2.0401-2017*  «CTPOl1TEJihHNI  KJil1MATOJIOfllil»  (SP  RK  2.04-01-2017*  «CONSTRUCTION CLIMATOLOGY»).
- long-term operation of the power plant at a frequency in the electrical network from 49 Hz to 51 Hz should be ensured. When the frequency drops to 4  7 Hz, the operating time of the power plant is at least  120 minutes. When the frequency increases to 51.5 Hz, the operating time of the power plant is at least 90 minutes.
- an automatic voltage regulation system should be provided to maintain the specified voltage level at the point of connection of  the power plant to the power system.
- -it  should  be  possible  to  start  the  units  from  emergency  and  system  automation  devices (including the automatic frequency and power control system (AFPCS).

Newly commissioned generating units with a maneuverable generation mode: must comply with the Requirements of the «Rules for organizing and conducting auctions for the construction of newly commissioned  generating  plants  with  a  maneuverable  generation  mode»  (Order  of the Ministry  of Energy of the Republic of  Kazakhstan No. 161 dated April 30, 2021), the requirements of  the Terms of reference.
The available volume of  regulating electric power,  which  will be  involved  in the  secondary regulation of  frequency and power flows, should provide:
- in the case of parallel operation of the UES of RK with the UES of Russia - maintaining the total  power flows  (balance of power  flows) for external communications  with  frequency  correction specified by the national dispatch center of the system operator of Kazakhstan;
- adjusting electric power is involved in automatic secondary regulation of  frequency and power;
- the volume of regulating electric power must correspond to the range of regulating electric power ofCCGT, +/- 50% of  P*. MW;
- the rate of change in the volume of  regulating electric power of generating installations for loading or unloading (corresponding to the regulation range) - at least 10 MW/min.;
- the involvement of  the regulating electric power in the automatic regulation of frequency and power is provided by the power plant without time and duration restrictions for the entire specified value of  the regulating electric power;
- it is possible to start and put into operation generating installations in the absence of  voltage in the external electrical network;
- generating installations allow the required number of  starts per year (at least 350 starts/year);
- the activation of the  regulating electric power for loading and unloading is carried out both promptly,  by  the  commands  of the  dispatching  personnel,  and  automatically  from  the  automatic frequency and power control system of the system operator.
The  requirements  for  the  control  range  for  the  newly  introduced  control  electric  power  of condensing combined-cycle plants that are not involved in heat supply are given in Table 2.6.1.
Table 2.6.1.

The main criteria for choosing an option for the construction of  a maneuverable power plant are:
- Providing electric power at the level of  1000 MW during the year;
- -Ensuring  the  maneuverability  of the  operation  of power  units  due  to  the  widest  range  of regulation;
- Ensuring the efficiency of  the power plant due to the high EF of  gas turbine units, and the steamgas cycle as a whole, a smaller decrease in the EF of  GT in the control range of  the power unit;
- Minimal decrease in power plant capacity during downtime of  power units for maintenance;
- Ensuring the reliability of  the power plant by installing industrially developed equipment.
The Shymkent region is characterized by hot summers with a maximum temperature of2'.:25 °C 141.  7 days, which requires the power plant to be provided both in winter and in summer.
The selected technology should ensure the operation of  power units in the control range without falling below the technical minimum, with shutdowns mainly only for maintenance.
The range of regulation depends on the season, the power of the GT is reduced in the summer and can be increased by installing evaporative cooling systems, optionally supplied with the GT.
When choosing the main equipment, it is necessary to be guided by the characteristics of  power units with a higher EF and the lowest cost.
At the same time, it should be taken into account that the withdrawal of one of the power units for maintenance or its emergency shutdown causes a loss of  power of  the power plant, the replacement of  power is problematic and depends on the availability of  reserve capacities in the power system.
Due to the fact that a single shutdown of  generation with a capacity of  more than 300 MW without the action of  the anti-emergency automatics (AEA) in the South Zone will lead to a violation of  stability, the maximum power of one generator of  the Facility should be up to 300 MW.
It is possible to use generators with a unit capacity of  up to 370 MW, provided that a balancing action is  organized to disconnect consumers in the amount of 100 MW from emergency automatics, triggered by the fact of an emergency shutdown of the generator, which should be provided for in the corresponding project.
The  advantages  of building  a  variant  of GT,  HRSG,  ST  are  determined  by  the  following parameters:
- Expected attestation power at the average January temperature (-1.5 °C) ~ MW;
- Expected regulation range (  expected base load minus the technical minimum) (-1.5 °C) during operation of the GT ~MW, when one GT is stopped, the range is reduced to ~MW;
- Possibility of bringing each unit  of generating equipment into repair while maintaining the remaining units of  generating equipment in operation.
Provide the layout of the main building of  power units.

List of technical documentation supplied together with the  HRSG:
- The  HRSG operation manual;
- List of documentation and installation drawings for installation;
- Auxiliary equipment operation manuals;
- Passport of the  HRSG (with applications in accordance with TPTC 032/2013 (TRTS 032/2013);
- Declaration of conformity or certificate of conformity  HRSG TPTC 032/2013 (TRTS 032/2013);
- Declaration of conformity or certificate of conformity of TRTS auxiliary equipment;
- Security justification.

Maintainability of heating surfaces, collectors and pipelines.
The heating surfaces of the  HRSG are made in the form of vertical packages suspended from the ceiling metal structures of the  HRSG using metal rods.
Between  the  rows  of  packages,  openings  of  at  least  1400  mm  are  organized,  designed  for inspection and repair of heating surfaces. In the upper and lower parts of the  HRSG, at the level of the section headers, horizontal  enclosing sheets are installed, forming with the ceiling and bottom of the boiler,  respectively,  the  upper  and  lower  «warm  boxes».  In  «warm  boxes»  repair  of  connecting manifolds and pipelines is provided, as well as disconnection of replaceable sections of heating surfaces from inlet and outlet pipes and enclosing structures.
Maintenance  personnel  have  access to  the  «warm  boxes»  and  to  the  gas  duct  to the heating surfaces through rectangular manholes in the shields of the gas-tight casing of the  HRSG. Maintenance personnel access to heating surfaces is organized using inventory rack scaffolding. For inspection and repair of the inner lining and insulation of the diffuser, as well as for inspection and repair of the flue to the chimney, manholes are arranged on the side  walls  for  access by maintenance personnel and the delivery of inventory scaffolding elements and other repair materials.
Manholes are  also  arranged  for  inspection  and repair  of  the  silencer,  shut-off valve  and flue compensator behind the  HRSG. Methods of control and testing at all stages of the manufacture ofHRSG elements provide a low probability of defects in pipes and welded joints during normal operation of the HRSG.
