The list of  electrical consumers of  the supplied equipment:
- -Pipe fittings and shut-off valve of  the chimney 30 kW;
- -Units (1 working, 1 standby) - 2xl  100 kW;
- -CGH recirculation pumps (1 working, 1 standby) 2x30 kW;
- -Drainage pump for pumping water from the BDT (1 working, 1 standby) - 2x15 kW;
- -Diverter sealing air fans - 2x45 kW;
- -Diverter electric drive 2x40 kV.

The following water treatment plants and facilities are envisaged:
- -WTP with a design capacity of  up to 340 m /h, for feeding HRSGs, starting low-pressure steam boilers, injection of  demineralized water into the combustion chamber of  gas turbines, feeding a closed cooling circuit and washing gas turbine compressors;
- -water treatment plant for the preparation of  drinking water with a design capacity of75 m 3 /h;
- -express laboratory of  WTP;
- -storage of  liquid reagents (acid, alkali, ammonia);
- -analytical express laboratory of  the main building;
- -wastewater neutralizer tanks from chemical washings of  boilers;
- -treatment facilities for oily wastewater with a capacity of  up to 50 m /h.
In order to meet the regulatory requirements for the quality of  feed water for drum HRSGs of two pressures, for the quality of  demineralized water for injection into the combustion chambers of  gas turbines, etc., a water treatment plant with a design capacity ofup to 340 m /h is provided.
Source  water  after  mechanical  filtration  on  self-cleaning  automatic  filters  undergoes  deep clarification at an ultrafiltration unit (UFU). Then the ultrafiltered water is supplied for desalination to the reverse osmosis units of  the first and second stages (ROU-1, II). Between ROU-1, II and ROU-11 to remove free carbon dioxide, the installation of  calciners is provided. Further, the desalinated water enters the electrodeionization units (EDU),  designed for deep desalination of  water to the required standard indicators for the feed water of  the HRSG.
Deeply desalinated (deionized) water after EDU is supplied for feeding steam recovery boilers, low-pressure steam boilers,  injection of desalted  water into the combustion chamber of  gas turbines, feeding a closed cooling circuit and washing gas turbine compressors.
Adjustment of  the pH of  deeply demineralized water with an ammonia solution is provided.
To  reduce the  consumption  of  initial  water and  the  output of  effluents,  reuse  of the  ROU-11
concentrate and EDU is provided.
For the preparation of  drinking water, a water treatment plant for the preparation of  drinking water with a design capacity of  75 m 3 /h is provided.
Source  water  after  mechanical  filtration  on  self-cleaning  automatic  filters  undergoes  deep clarification on UFU. Then the ultra-filtered water enters for demineralization at the ROU in one stage. Demineralized water after ROU is sent to ultraviolet sterilization units for final disinfection of  water and then supplied for drinking needs.

Gas from the main gas pipelines is used as the main fuel at the Facility, diesel fuel is used as an emergency fuel.
The following fuel facilities and auxiliary buildings are provided at the power plant site:
- Gas treatment plant;
- Diesel fuel warehouse with pumping station;
- Oil apparatus with oil storage;
- Air compressor station.

From the  station  fence  to  the  gas  treatment  plant,  a  gas  pipeline  is  being  laid,  on  which  an electrified disconnecting valve is placed with a shelter from weather conditions and a service platform.
The  gas  treatment  plant  includes  block-complete  equipment,  consisting  of the  following technological units of  full factory readiness:
- gas consumption metering station (GCMS): a measurement unit with flow meters and filters for cleaning all gas entering the station;
- block  gas  control  point  (GCP):  a  reduction  unit  for  supplying  gas  to  start-up  boilers  via  a medium-pressure gas pipeline;
- container for collecting high pressure condensate;
- -nitrogen ramp in cover.

Diesel fuel grade Z-0.2-40 according to fOCT 305-82 (GOST 305-82) is used as emergency fuel for gas turbines at the station.
The following buildings and structures are envisaged:
- -diesel fuel warehouse;
- -diesel fuel pumping station.
The capacity of  the diesel fuel storage used as a reserve is taken into account the operation of  all GT at their rated load for 3 days. For the storage of  diesel fuel, ground steel tanks should be provided, the capacity to be determined by the project.
A diesel fuel pumping station is provided for receiving and pumping diesel fuel. The following equipment is located in the pump room:
- -main (fuel) pumps - working and reserve, supplying diesel fuel from storage tanks to the CCGT building;
- -pumps for pumping diesel fuel from the drain device to the warehouse - working and standby;
- -pumping pumps from drainage pits  - working and reserve;
- -pump for pumping fuel from the bottom layers of  tanks.
- Filters are provided on the suction pipelines of  the main and unloading pumps.

To receive, store and supply oil to the main building of  the CCGT, an oil equipment room and an oil warehouse are provided at the site.
The oil pumping station is located in the same building as the diesel fuel pumping station. The following equipment is installed in the oil chamber:
- -oil intake pump with a coarse filter installed in front of  it;
- -transfer pump (main);
- -mobile installation for cleaning and regeneration of  oil;
- -drainage pump.
Six tanks for used, fresh and regenerated oil, with a capacity of70m 3 each, are installed in the oil storage in the dike.
Two fresh oil storage tanks are designed to receive marketable oil from the transport tank and store the necessary supply of  fresh oil.
Two storage tanks for regenerated (purified) oil are designed to receive and store oil after it has been processed in the oil equipment room in order to prepare it for filling into equipment. These tanks can be used as a backup for receiving and storing fresh oil, as well as for receiving operating oil drained from the equipment during repairs, which can be refilled into the equipment.
Two waste oil storage tanks are designed to collect and store oil sent for regeneration or disposal.

To deliver power, it is necessary to build a new 500/220/10 kV substation of  a new maneuverable power plant.
The  substation  provides  for  the  installation  of one  group  of single-phase  autotransformers 500/220/10 kV with a capacity of not less  than  167 MV  A with the installation of a reserve (back-up) phase.
To supply power from the generators of the designed CCGTs, it is planned to install step-up three-phase transformers in accordance with nominal output voltages of  the generator.
10  kV  SG  is  provided  from  metal  cabinets  complete  SG (CSG)  type  with  vacuum  circuit breakers. The project provides for the installation of  3(three) CSG -10 kV cabinets, including:
- 1 - introductory;
- 1 - for power supply of  the auxiliary transformer;
- 1 - for connecting a voltage transformer;
A block-modular building is provided for the placement of  CSG-1  0kV cabinets.
A block-modular building is provided for the placement oflow-voltage complete devices 0.4 kV, Relay protection  and  automation (RP  A),  Automated  control  system  (ACS), Monitoring  and control system (MCS) and Dispatching and technological control system (DTCS) cabinets. The modules are transportable  prefabricated  blocks with  equipment,  apparatus  and devices of the  main  and  auxiliary circuits, fully assembled inside, with lighting, heating, ventilation and air conditioning systems, with fire and burglar alarms, and grounding. Blocks are mounted on the foundation.
To supply auxiliary needs of  6 kV, in the taps of  blocks switched to 220/500 kV, transformers of the working power supply are installed, with a capacity of  not less than 16000 kVA. ASG 6 kV of  the main building consists of  six aggregate sections. The work of  the sections is provided according to the «explicit  reserve»  scheme.  The  backup  power  supply  of the  sections  is  provided from  two  backup transformers  with  a  capacity  of not  less  than  16,000  kVA  and  a  voltage  of 220/6.3  kV.  Backup transformers are connected to different sections of  220kV SG.

The implementation of the generator circuit within the main building, as well as between the main building and the block transformer, is provided for by complete current conductors of  the generator voltages in the range of  10-30 kV.
The block circuit provides for the installation of  a generator switch.
As a generator circuit breaker, it is planned to use a gas-insulated distribution generator device. The composition of  the sulphur hexafluoride gas distribution generator set includes:
- sulphur hexafluoride circuit breaker;
