In terms of  the MCP of  the station, taking into account modem requirements for the introduction of automated production control systems, an automated control system (ACS-MCP) is provided. ACS­ MCP is built on the basis of  a hardware and software complex (HSC). The HSC of  ACS-MCP system meets the requirements of  technical safety at power plants and is designed in such a way that erroneous actions of  operational personnel and failures of  technical means do not lead to situations dangerous to life and health of people. The system is implemented on the basis of  programmable logic controllers. In the MCP room, two automated workstations (AWS) of shift-supervisor of  the power plant (SSPP) and shift-supervisor of  the electrical workshop SSEW are installed to control electrical equipment and an automated workstation of  a relay engineer in the relay team room.
The ACS-MCP system is designed to monitor,  control,  display, signal and record physical and electrical parameters and discrete signals the main electrical equipment of the station. The system is a functionally and geographically distributed structure that uses several independent local boards or nodes containing control processors, power supplies, data transmission systems. Local boards are able to work autonomously and perform data  collection,  calculation, control functions of switching devices. Data transmission between nodes and at workstations of operators and engineers located in the main control room is provided through specially designed, redundant high-speed data transmission lines.
ACS-MCP provides the following functions:
- Control of generator-transformer units;
- Element Management 220kV;
- Condition control by generators;
- Spinning reserve monitoring;
- Load distribution;
- Load shedding;
- Registration of  alarms and events;
- Registration and analysis of  archival data;
- DC installations.
The MCP provides for manual, automatic synchronization for 220kV circuit breakers.

