The following hierarchical levels are  distinguished vertically in  the technical structure of the APCS:
The upper level is the level of  visualization and operational management (SCADA - Supervisory Control  And  Data  Acquisition)  the  level  of  information  presentation,  operational  control  and management, analysis of current and retrospective information. It is located in the MCP and consists of workstations - servers for processing and storing information, equipment for network components, A  WS of operational and maintenance personnel, and provides an interface for interaction between personnel and the control system. The A  WS of  the boiler room operator uses a SCAD  A system. The A  WS provides convenient and effective control by the operator over the performance of all information, control and service functions of  the ACS.
The operator's A  WS is designed to visualize process parameters, remotely control actuators, enter tasks for regulators,  view individual protocols, reports and summaries, enable or disable control subsystems (autoregulation, AWS, switchable interlocks) and perform other functions. On the computer of the  operator's AWS, the programs of the application server operate, which is the main connecting element of information flows between the software of the upper and lower (Software controller) levels of  the system.
Top-level Software system includes:
- SCAD  A package software;
- -The  software  below  for  each  component  of  the  circuit  gives  a  brief description  of the characteristics and purpose.
The middle level - the level of control and management (Control Level, PLC (PLC)) - includes control  systems  for the  main  and  auxiliary  equipment  based  on a  redundant  software  and hardware automation complex with the possibility of  hot replacement, as well as automatic control systems (ACS) supplied complete with process equipment, performs algorithmic processing of information from sensors and primary signal converters and the formation of control actions on actuators and regulatory bodies, as well as diagnostics of  peripheral equipment.
The controller is an element of the system that provides connection of cable connections from sensors and conversion of  analog signals from sensors into digital form (ADC code) necessary for further software  processing  by  the  system.  The  digitized  information  from  the  sensors  undergoes  primary processing inside the controllers for:
- conversion to engineering units;
- calculation of  derived quantities (pressure, temperature, flow rates, etc.);
- analysis of the reliability of  the measured values;
- formation of an Instantaneous Database corresponding to the current values of the measured values, which are available at any time for controller programs;
- updating values for upper-level subsystems - sending special telegrams about changes in values, achievement of warning,  emergency and other settings, and fulfillment of other criteria for updating information of  the «upper» level.

Operational and tariff accounting should be provided for process control, electricity quantity, performance control and emissions control. The measured data should be used for billing, process control and monitoring  purposes  as  required  and  described  below.  The  data  must  be  obtained  from  factory instruments  designed  and  installed  to measure actual values  and,  if necessary,  must be corrected for changes in pressure, temperature, density, etc.
