Consumers of all  groups,  except  for  computer  equipment,  should be divided into subgroups according  to  the  technological  principle:  for  the  boiler  and  turbine  departments.  Distribution  into subgroups, groups should be carried out through independent protection devices that provide selective shutdown of damaged areas and repair of  power supply network elements without stopping the main equipment.
The power supply of all devices of the hardware and software complex  (HSC) must be provided from their own power sources  (modules).
The primary power sources of the HSC can be two independent networks, each of which is a three-phase  AC  network  380/220  V,  frequency  50±1  Hz.  Characteristics  of  primary  power  supply networks:
- rated linear voltage - 380 V  (+  10, -15%);
- rated phase voltage - 220 V  (  +  10, ~  15%  );
- number of  phases - 3.
The primary power sources of the HSC can also be two independent networks, one of which is a three-phase alternating current network with a voltage of 380/220 V, a frequency of (50 ± 1) Hz, and the other is a direst current network with a voltage of 220 V. Power supplies for devices of  the HSC lower level  (for example, controller cabinets) can be designed to receive power from two independent networks (according to one of the above options), or from only one network. In this case, the devices of the lower level of  the HSC should be powered by uninterruptible power supplies  (UPS). The UPS must be powered from two independent networks (two alternating current networks or one alternating current network, the other direct current). It is preferable to include UPS in the delivery ofHSC.
Technical means must remain operational when:

- independent or simultaneous changes in the voltage of the alternating current and direct current networks by ±25% for up to 100 ms when the HSC is powered from the alternating current and direct current mains;
- during long interruptions in the power supply in one of  the alternating current or direct current networks when the HSC is powered from the alternating current and direct current networks;
- during long interruptions in the power supply in one of the two alternating current networks when the HSC is powered from two alternating current networks;
- during simultaneous interruptions of power supply with a duration of not more than 20 ms in two networks.
The HSC devices must be protected against reverse polarity direct current voltage supply. The HSC devices should not be damaged or falsely triggered when one of  the two primary power supply networks is connected and  (or) disconnected.
The  power  supply  of  the  HSC  devices,  which  implement  the  functions  of  technological protection,  must be  carried  out with the highest reliability from an alternating current source with a voltage of380/220 V, a frequency of(50 ± 1) Hz, with a battery backup. The operability of  devices that implement the functions of technological protection must be ensured in the presence of  a voltage of  the specified quality at least on one of the two inputs, as well as in case of short-term  (up to 5.0 s) deviations of  the supply voltage within(+  15, -30%) and frequency up to ±5 Hz. In case of  ARI of the supply voltage with a voltage loss for a time of  at least 0.5 s, false alarms of  the protections should not occur.
The power supply of duplicated HSC devices must be provided from independent sources.
The power supply of technical means of  the upper level of  the HSC, sufficient for a trouble-free shutdown of  the equipment, must be provided from uninterruptible power supplies  (UPS) with internal battery support  (up to 30 minutes). These UPSs can be powered from a 220 V alternating current source, 50 Hz uninterruptible power supply (via ARI), or from two independent alternating current 220 V, 50 Hz networks. Uninterruptible power supply devices should be included in the scope of  delivery of the HSC. The UPS power supply of operator stations included in one A  WS and reserving each other must
be provided from independent sources of  primary power supply. In this case, it is allowed to power the UPS from one source of primary power supply with a voltage of 220 V, a frequency of  50 Hz.

