Power  plants  must  be  equipped  with  starting  systems,  flushing  systems,  fire  protection  and housings.
The automatic fire extinguishing system of the power plant must comply with the norms and requirements of  the Republic of  Kazakhstan.
A sufficient number of  fire detectors and spray nozzles must be provided in each compartment of  the unit.  It is necessary to provide an alarm signal (remotely and locally) that allows the operating personnel to leave the installation before the fire extinguishing system is automatically activated. The system must be equipped with a switch in order to tum off the unit at the right time if  necessary.
All  compartments  of the installations must have adequate lighting,  as  well as  ventilation and heating.
Sufficient access openings, walkways, etc. should be provided. for the possibility of  performing maintenance work on the components of  power plants.
Particular attention should be paid to the need to ensure that basic maintenance  work can be carried out easily. It shall be possible to use lifting equipment for inspection and maintenance work.
It shall be possible to carry out inspections using an endoscope on the power plant units, as well as, if  necessary, the use of  barring devices and a stepping inductor motor. All equipment for endoscopic examinations  and all  instruments  necessary  for  opening  and  closing  holes  must  be  included  in  the delivery.
To determine the performance of  power plants under actual external conditions and various loads, the following graphs should be included in the technical documentation:
dependence of  power on the outdoor temperature;
dependence of  efficiency on power at various outdoor temperatures;
dependence of fuel consumption on power at various outdoor temperatures;
dependence of exhaust gas consumption on power at various outdoor temperatures;
dependence  of the  coefficient  of excess  air  in  the  exhaust  gases  on  the  power  at  different temperatures of the outside air;
dependence of exhaust gas temperature on power at different outdoor air temperatures;
dependence of  the relative values of  power, fuel consumption, temperature and exhaust gas flow on changes in total pressure losses in the inlet device;

The fuel supply system of power plants must ensure a complete shutdown of the fuel supply when the controlled operating parameters go beyond the permissible values. Valves must be properly sealed in the closed position. Check valves must be locally and remotely operated.
Protective  devices  must  have  priority  effect  on  the  control  valves  when  performing  partial unloading or complete shutdown, depending on the degree of danger of the conditions created.  These valves must also be affected by the emergency overspeed mechanism.
The necessary number of contacts must be provided for remote indicators of the position of  the stop valves and for transmitting a signal to  disconnect  the generator  from the network when they are closed.
Power installations must be equipped with protections that immediately tum off the installation in cases stipulated by the technical operating conditions.
The control system of power plants must meet the following requirements:
sustainably maintain a given electrical load;
maintain power plants idling at the nominal rotor speed;
ensure reliable operation of power plants in start-up and shutdown modes, as well as shutdown of  the unit in emergency situations;
ensure, when the load changes, a smooth change in the operating mode of  power plants;
maintain the rotor speed, which does not trigger the safety switch, with an instantaneous reset of the maximum load to zero;
ensure the stable operation of  the compressor;
have  a  degree  of static  non-uniformity  of regulation  of the  rotation  frequency  of the  shaft generator within 2% of  the nominal;
have a degree of  insensitivity at any load not more than 0.2% of  the rated speed.
The capacity and duration of operation of power plants with deviations from the normal speed should be regulated by the manufacturer's specifications.
Safety breakers must be adjusted to operate when the rotor speed increases by 10-12% above the nominal value or to the value specified in the manufacturer's specifications.
The  characteristic  of the  control  system  and  the  description  of all  devices  intended  for  the protection of power plants in conditions beyond the permissible ones must be detailed and illustrated with drawings, sketches and diagrams.
The  regulation  system  must  be  accompanied  by  a  manual  for  the  repair  and  adjustment  of equipment, including repair forms, testing and adjustment procedures.
A set of spare parts,  tools,  accessories and materials (SPT  AM) for the control and protection system must be determined  and included in the supply of  equipment.
Control regulators must automatically regulate the supply of  fuel to power plants from a state of no load to a state of  maximum power. There should be a mechanism for setting the load speed of  power plants.
The control valve must operate in such a way that there is no overspeed and speed fluctuation over the entire load range.  The temporary increase in speed due to the  instantaneous release  of the maximum load shall not be such as to cause the stop-check valves to actuate.

Contractor provides bearings locations;
Bearings data:
- -bearing type;
- -bearing inner diameter;
- -bearing length;
- -number, location and geometry of pillows;
- -preload of each bearing pad;
- -brand of  antifriction material;
- -ISO brand and characteristics of  supplied lubricants.
The Contractor determines the operating temperature range of the machine bearings.
The level of  absolute vibration of  the bearings or stator elements of  the unit, characterized by the rms value of  the vibration velocity, must, upon acceptance of  the unit into operation and during its further operation, comply with the requirements of GOST ISO 10816-4-2002.
All bearings of power plants must be designed in such a way that it is possible to center the bearings without opening the unit. Alignment shims or similar means must be supplied for subsequent adjustment of the horizontal  and  vertical  position  of the  bearings  to  eliminate  misalignment  due  to settlement of foundations or for other reasons.  A device must be provided to relieve the bearing from the  weight  of the shaft during the  extraction  operation.  Means  must be provided to  prevent  oil from flowing along the shaft.
Thrust bearings must be segment type. If they are not, then the Contractor shall note this feature and provide evidence that the proposed bearing type performs reliably under comparable loads.  The bearing support ring must be in a position that provides maximum relative expansions and clearances in the constituent elements of the unit, and it must be possible to periodically adjust them. Thrust bearings must have both thrust and bearing surfaces.  The entire design of the unit must ensure the absence of reversible axial forces in all modes of  operation up to the maximum load.
