Lubricating oil must be supplied to the bearings at a pressure sufficient to form a hydrodynamic film during the acceleration of  the rotor to the rated speed. Pressure gauges must be installed on the distribution manifold  of the  oil lines.  To  control  the oil temperature,  temperature  sensors  should be provided at the drain from each bearing, and alarms should be provided when this temperature rises. The oil temperature in the  distribution manifold downstream of  the  oil  coolers must be controlled, and an increase  or  decrease  in  temperature  beyond  the  established  limits  must  actuate  the  alarm  means. Provision must also be made to measure the temperature of  each thrust bearing and thrust bearing at a sufficient number of  points to accurately monitor their condition.
Downstream of the oil coolers, oil filters with differential pressure sensors for alarms and, in addition, an additional filter for the thrust bearing must be provided. The pressure of  the oil entering the bearings must be measured in the common distribution manifold, as well as after the individual thrust bearing filter. All filters must have individual bypasses and be accessible for cleaning while the unit is under load.

The equipment  must  be  designed  taking  into  account  the  requirements  of the  Rules  for  the technical operation of  power plants and networks and the existing regulatory-, technical and legislative documentation  on  safety,  explosion  and  fire  safety  in  force  on  the  territory  of the  Republic  of Kazakhstan.
In the event of  an emergency, the safety of  the operating personnel must be ensured. Mechanical safety must be ensured:
- design of  power plants, including heat and sound insulating shelters;
- blocking and protective devices that prevent power plants from going beyond the established limit values of  parameters;
- the presence of  protective covers on the rotating parts of  the equipment of  the power plant, the design  and  placement  of parts  and  assembly  units,  excluding  the  possibility  of injury  to  the  plant operating personnel during operation.
Explosion and fire safety must be ensured:
- the use  of non-combustible  or hardly  combustible structural  materials,  insulating  and paint coatings that do not contribute to the spread of  fire;
- adjustment of  pipelines of  oil, fuel and air systems of  power plants from resonant vibrations in the entire range of  operating modes;
- exclusion of  explosive accumulations of  oil-air mixture, gas and liquid fuel in the elements of power plants;
- ventilation of  the gas-air path of  power plants before launch;
- the presence of  fittings for the supply of  extinguishing agent from the fire extinguishing system and the installation of  fire alarm sensors in the heat and sound insulating shelter of  power plants, in the generator and the block of  electrical equipment;
- implementation of  electrical equipment, taking into account the requirements for fire safety for the premises of  the engine room (shelters);
- the location of  the units of  the oil system of  power plants, excluding their unacceptable heating; - measures in accordance with the operating instructions for power plants and compliance with the requirements of  manufacturers.
Thermal and toxicological safety of  power plants should be ensured by:
- the presence of  thermal insulation, the temperature on the surface, which should not exceed 45 °C at an ambient temperature of  plus 25 ° C;
- the presence of  a ventilation and cooling system;
- power plant units of  materials that do not emit toxic substances in all operating modes and in the non-working state above the maximum permissible concentrations.
The  design  of power  plants  and  the  automatic  control  system  must  ensure  the  normal  safe operation of  the plant without the constant presence of maintenance personnel.
The Contractor must provide a description of all measures to ensure fire safety in the premises of power plants.

Power plants must remain operational under the following conditions:
- -ambient temperature from minus 40 °C to plus 50 °C;
- -barometric pressure from 84.0 kPa to 110 kPa;
- -relative air humidity up to 98% (at +25 °C).
Protective, decorative and  paint  coatings  should  ensure  the  safety  of surfaces  and  corrosion resistance of parts and assembly units during storage and operation.

