Engineering and geological  surveys  for the  implementation of Works on the  Facility should provide a comprehensive study of the engineering and geological conditions of the area (site, section, route) of  the planned construction of  the Facility, including the relief, geological structure, geomorphological  and  hydrogeological  conditions,  composition,  condition  and  properties  of soils, geological and engineering - geological processes, changes in the  conditions  of developed  (built-up) territories,  forecasting  of possible  changes  in  engineering  and  geological  conditions  in  the  field  of interaction of  the designed objects with the geological environment in order to obtain the necessary and sufficient materials for the design, construction and operation of the Facility.
Engineering and geological surveys should provide a comprehensive study of the engineering and  geological  conditions  of the  area  (site,  section,  route)  of the  designed  power transmission line, including relief,  geological structure, composition, condition and properties of soils.
The composition of engineering and geological surveys includes:
- collection and processing of  materials from surveys and studies of  past years;
- decryption of  aero- and space materials;
- reconnaissance survey, including aero-visual and route observations;
- tunneling of mine workings;
- geophysical surveys;
- field studies of  soils;
- hydrogeological research;
- stationary observations (local monitoring of the components of the geological environment);
- laboratory studies of  soils, underground and surface waters;
- survey of  soils of  the bases of  the foundations of existing buildings and structures;
- making a forecast of changes in engineering and geological conditions;
