«Automated Completion System». Electronic database of equipment numbers, class A, B and C inspections required,  inspection date, items of the Defect list,  etc.  The database should be organized subsystemically,  according  to  the  systemic  (by  functionally  nodal)  approach  will  become  the  main source of registration and reporting on the status of completion of construction and the progress of the PCW.

The Mechanical readiness of facilities is considered achieved if:
1. Works  are  completed in  accordance  with  the  Contract,  including  in accordance  with  the provisions specified in  the  terms  of the  Contract,  including defects, with the exception of defects in accordance  with  Items  of  the  Defect  list  of C  category  and  Items  of the  Defect  list  of  D  category, specified in the Defect list;
2. Works meet all the requirements of  the applicable legislation of  the RK;
3. The facilities are built in accordance with the applicable drawings and specifications set out in the Contract;
4. The facilities satisfy the requirements that determine the achievement of  Mechanical readiness specified in  this  section,  the related tests  and procedures  are  performed  with a  satisfactory  result in accordance with the additional procedure agreed by the parties;
5. Eliminated all defects according to Items of the Defect list of A category and Items of the Defect list of  B category;
6. The Contractor has provided a list of  all existing bonds and undertakes to indemnify and hold harmless the Customer from any claims for such bonds.
The list  of types  of work  related to Mechanical  readiness  to  be determined jointly  with the Customer, after the approval of  the design and estimate documentation.
If  the Contractor considers that the requirements that determine the achievement of Mechanical readiness set forth in this section are fulfilled, the Contractor shall notify the Customer in writing and request the Customer to issue a Mechanical readiness certificate.
Within 14 days after receiving a request from the Contractor, the Customer undertakes:
- issue to the Contractor a Mechanical readiness  certificate, indicating the date on which the facilities reached Mechanical readiness in accordance with the Contract;
- reject the request, stating the reasons and indicating the work to be performed by the Contractor in order to obtain the Mechanical readiness certificate. Subject to its obligations to carry out such Works, the Contractor shall complete the Works prior to further notice under this Section.

