All  persons  associated  with  this  project  must work  without  injury,  without  the  influence  of alcohol and drugs,  and must comply with the Customer's safety requirements, as well as all applicable codes and standards of  the RK.
The Contractor is responsible for initiating, maintaining and overseeing all Occupational Health and  Safety  (OH&S)  and  environmental  safeguards  and  programs  in  connection  with  the  work.  The Contractor  shall provide  a  safety  program, OH&S  policies,  an  occupational  health  and  safety management system, risk assessment and management adapted to the Project.
The Contractor's health, safety and environmental program shall provide for frequent and regular inspections of  work sites, materials and equipment by competent persons in the field of OH&S (capable of  identifying  existing  and  predicted  hazards  in  the  environment  or  working  conditions  that  are unsanitary, harmful or hazardous to workers and who are authorized to take prompt corrective action to address them).
The Contractor is responsible for providing and maintaining safe and healthy working conditions for  its  employees,  as  well  as  other  project  participants  and  the  public.  Thus,  the  responsibility  for correcting or, the cost of correcting unsafe practices or conditions remains with the Contractor.
The Contractor shall develop and submit to the Customer for approval its «Specific OH&S plan for the project» which shall include, but not be limited to:
- 1) Work production plan;
- 2) Identified hazards, risk assessment and their management;
- 3) Control over the work;
- 4) Identification of inconsistencies and measures to eliminate them.

1. The Contractor is responsible for providing and maintaining a safe, non-hazardous and healthy  workplace  for  its  employees,  employees  of its  subcontractors,  the  Customer, interested parties, visitors and the general public.
The Contractor shall ensure health and safety measures at all stages of the project and comply with all  applicable  laws,  rules,  regulations  and  standards  of the Republic  of Kazakhstan, as well as international best practice in the field of safety, including:
- a) general medical examination before employment;
- b) special pre-employment medical examination and a check for suitability for a particular position;
- c) periodic health checks of  workers;
- d) pre-shift and pre-trip medical examination of employees involved in the maintenance and operation of  hazardous technical devices and mechanisms;
- e) vaccination programs;
- f) other types of disease prevention that are global in nature or specific to the area where the project is being implemented.
- g) organizing the provision of first aid and a medical center.

The Contractor will develop and implement a personnel management policy and principles of human resources management in accordance with the labor legislation of the RK and the requirements of the International Labor Organization  (ILO). This plan will detail labor requirements for the entire construction period, the Contractor's local recruitment process, and the planned approach to maximize local employment opportunities. Human resources policy and principles of  human resource management will cover the following issues:
- equal rights, equal pay;
- a ban on all forms of child and forced labor;
- rights and obligations of employees (including the Code of conduct for employees);
- freedom of association in trade unions and the right to conduct collective bargaining;
- informing employees about their rights, duties, responsibilities and privileges;
- the terms of the employment contract,  including  the terms of employment, hours  of work, overtime and related compensation, as well as the right to refuse requests for overtime.

